 "notes": [
  "Footnote items after tax sum to 24 vs printed aggregate 23 (rounding); items_total_net keeps 23.",
  "Indices operating profit attributable to the Company $105m; adjusted OP attributable $106m (NCI $38m).",
  "Adjusted Corporate Unallocated Expense excluding adjusted Kensho expense ($13m): $27m. Adjusted total expense $775m; adjusted ETR 18.3%.",
  "Cash flow and FCF are full-year (ytd_months 12).",
  "Intersegment royalty charged by Ratings to Market Intelligence: $28m.",
  "Q4-18 release restates 2017 comparatives (pension ASU 2017-07 and segment reclass): e.g. FY2017 MI revenue 1,683 vs 1,678 originally, Indices 728 vs 733; 2017 balance sheet RNCI 1,352 / total equity 766 vs 1,350 / 768 originally.",
  "Pension related charge $5m ($4m after-tax) is now below operating profit (other income) -> seg NONOP, cat NONOP; adj_oth_inc = adjusted other income, net (income +).",
  "items_total_pre = the printed Total SPGI operating-profit non-GAAP adjustments only; the $5m other-income (pension) adjustment is printed separately (items_total_pre_nonop).",
  "Kensho retention related expense categorised ACQ; lease impairments IMPAIR.",
  "From Q2-18 a \"Corporate\" revenue line (Kensho) is printed in the segment table and Corporate Unallocated is shown net of it. seg_other.corp = Corporate Unallocated operating loss as printed (net of corporate revenue, positive cost); corp_rev = Corporate revenue; corp_exp = Corporate Unallocated expense. check_rec \"sum seg rev + elim = rev\" therefore differs by corp_rev (not a transcription error): segments + elim + corp_rev = total revenue.",
  "cfpub capex and nci_dist recorded as positive cash costs (release prints them in brackets). fcf_items signed as printed (added to FCF to reach FCF excluding certain items).",
  "rev_type key ELIM = intersegment elimination; CORP = Corporate revenue.",
  "py_seg = Q4-17 comparative on the 2018 basis. Differs from as-reported and from the Q1-18 recast: MI revenue 441 (vs 440), Indices revenue 190 (vs 191) - a $1m MI/Indices reclass; MI OP 123 / adj 145 (vs 126 / 146 in Q1-18 recast) and Indices OP 122 / adj 123 (vs 119 / 122); deal amortization MI 19 / Indices 1 (vs 17 / 3). Total OP 627 vs 628 as reported; segment total and revenue totals unchanged (1,589).",
  "py_seg adjusted OP sums to 791 vs printed adjusted segment total 790 (company rounding)."
 ],
